    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d873">

                <pb facs="1083" n="959" xml:id="pg959"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7451/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">DNC 12479–1072:43</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information in connection with the unsigned memorandum of Department of State
                    dated 14 December, 1920,<anchor n="51" xml:id="d873-f1"/> on the subject of
                    reciprocal rights for the Lafayette Radio Station, a copy of a proposed
                    agreement drawn up in a conference between Rear Admiral Bullard of this
                    Department and Monsieur Broin and General Ferrié of the French
                        delegation.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d873-f2"/></p>
                <p>Monsieur Broin of the French delegation has a copy of the proposed agreement and
                    upon his return to France the question of its ratification by the French
                    Department of Posts and Telegraphs will be taken up by him. Unless or until
                    further information as to the action taken by the French Department of Posts and
                    Telegraphs is received, it is not believed that any further steps are necessary
                    on the part of this Government.</p>
                <p>Please accept my thanks for the co-operation and assistance rendered by the
                    Department of State in connection with this matter.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d873-a1.xml" xpointer="d873-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
